---
import Cover from '../layouts/Cover.astro';
---

<Cover
  title="Method"
  description="How Noemium grades tools: ship / situational / skip. A PR is the unit of truth."
  page="method"
>
  <div class="cover-doc">
    <section class="cover-lede">
      <h1>Method</h1>
      <p>Ship, situational, skip. A pull request is the unit of truth.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="cover-doors">
      <div class="cover-door">
        <b>Ship</b>
        <span>We run it and would run it again for this job.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cover-door">
        <b>Situational</b>
        <span>Wins in a named setup. Loses outside it.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cover-door">
        <b>Skip</b>
        <span>We would pick something else for the same job.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="cover-prose">
      <h2>Receipts</h2>
      <p>A URL behind every printed fact. No source, no number.</p>

      <h2>Verification</h2>
      <p>
        Source-verified means receipts. Field-tested means we ran it. The{' '}
        <a href="/verified/">verified shelf</a> is field-tested only.
      </p>

      <h2>No stars</h2>
      <p>We don't average vibes. Wrong? Edit the page.</p>

      <h2>Paid placements</h2>
      <p>
        Zero. Affiliates are declared. Declined offers live in the{' '}
        <a href="/refusals/">refusal ledger</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/about/">About</a>
        {' · '}
        <a href="/contribute/">Contribute</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Cover>
